  "notes": [
    {
      "at": [
        -35,
        -23
      ],
      "id": 26,
      "text": "ATmega8A with a 16 MHz crystal between XTAL1 and XTAL2 (and 22 pF to ground, as on a breadboard): the fuses\nlow EF, high C9 select it (CKSEL 1111, CKOPT). avr_blink_16mhz blinks the LED on PB0 once a second.\nSet the low fuse back to E1 (internal 1 MHz) or remove the crystal to see what a student's chip does."
    }
  ],
